From 091c37accf1fb02f35935f18af11d5fcf2a20d07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:40:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(panel): stop identifying applet plugins by their
 translated name

since the plugin names became translatable in #986, peas_plugin_info_get_name
returns the localized name. the plugin manager used it to match the name stored
in each applet's settings, so in a translated locale every applet whose name has
a translation failed to load and was dropped from the panel. budgie_applet_info_new
also wrote the localized name back into the applet's settings.

applets now store the plugin's module name in a new optional module key, which
the loader prefers. without it, the untranslated Name is read from the .plugin
file, since libpeas only exposes the localized one, and the localized name is
still accepted so configs saved by 10.10.3 load. on load, the module key is
filled in and a localized name is replaced with the untranslated one, with a
message logged per applet. the localized name is kept as display-name for the
applets list in settings.

panel.ini entries gain Module=, preferred over ID= when present.

add_new loads the plugin and creates the applet directly, since modprobe is
synchronous. the creating table matched applets to the extension-loaded signal
by the name add_new was given, which is localized from the chooser or a module
from panel.ini, so it never matched the untranslated name the signal carries.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
